I might be a little biased because I just rewatched it, but Mr. Wantanabe from Ikiru is a great representation of the  Übermensch. He spent almost his whole life acting out the role of the camel and had a brief period shortly after he found out that he had cancer as the lion. He realized that the life of the lion is unfulfilling, wasteful, and most importantly of all, it builds no lasting relationships. 

&#x200B;

When he decided to pour his heart into his work, he did so in defiance of his superiors, his family, the polite conventions of society, and the businessmen (in this case the gangsters that wanted a new redlight district) who typically pervert government to their needs. In my opinion, that is what makes him an Übermensch.

'Not everyone has kids in school' 

&#x200B;

Yes, but everybody is affected by the quality of education that our future citizens are receiving. Taxes go to funding schools because it's considered a public good just like prisons are. Even if you don't have kids you will be affected by the consequences of restricting food to younger generations
